1. Chromium Embedded Framework 156 and Chromium
===============================================

Bundled: the CEF 156 minimal binary distribution for Linux and the Chromium 156
build inside it, from the distribution dated 2026-10-24, with symbol tables
stripped as described below:

  CEF version        156.0.14+g4fa4ab5+chromium-156.0.8078.48
  CEF commit         4fa4ab516dacf6c49fc7e6e70d2b7ebce29fa35f
                     https://github.com/chromiumembedded/cef
  Chromium version   156.0.8078.48
  Chromium commit    d0c02bfad08ec92a6ffcf989e53cd995e6381a4c
                     https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src

Licence: BSD 3-Clause. The text, with the copyright holders' names, is
cef-LICENSE.txt. Chromium's own copyright holders and the third-party licences
inside the runtime are listed in cef-CREDITS.html.gz, which is the authoritative
list for the engine, shipped gzip-compressed the way /usr/share/doc prose
usually is (zcat it).

What was changed: the files are the distribution's bytes. libcef.so has its
symbol table stripped with `strip --strip-unneeded` (1.48 GB to 277 MB) so the
install fits its size budget; no code is changed, added or removed, and every
other file in the directory is copied as it is. Checked file by file against
the distribution: the nine data and helper files and the three locale archives
are byte-identical, and libcef.so differs only by that symbol table.

Only part of the distribution is shipped: the runtime library, the data files
it reads at startup (resources.pak, chrome_100_percent.pak,
chrome_200_percent.pak, icudtl.dat, v8_context_snapshot.bin,
libvk_swiftshader.so, libvulkan.so.1, vk_swiftshader_icd.json, chrome-sandbox)
and the locales for en-US, en-GB and hi. The headers, the CMake files and the
other 217 locales are not shipped.

2. Node.js 22
=============

Bundled: usr/lib/rook/node, a Node.js official Linux binary, v22.23.4. Its
symbol table is stripped and nothing else about it is changed; the code is
upstream's. Checked by stripping the release binary again, which reproduces the
shipped file byte for byte. The version is what the bundled interpreter reports
for `--version`.

Licence: MIT, plus the licences of the projects statically bundled into the
binary (V8, OpenSSL, npm, libuv, zlib and others). node-LICENSE is Node's own
LICENSE file from that release, which carries all of them in one text.
Upstream: https://nodejs.org/ , https://github.com/nodejs/node

3. The ego-browser SDK
======================

Bundled: usr/lib/rook/sdk/, a build of the ego-browser agent skill and SDK by
CitroLabs, from the upstream commit Rook is developed against:

  version     v2.1.0-6-gaecc583  (git describe)
  commit      aecc5831fc5a9ea01a078b632185992a3a7ac448
  package     package/ego-browser in that commit

Licence: MIT, copyright (c) 2026 CitroLabs. sdk-LICENSE is the upstream LICENSE
file at that commit, byte for byte; its SHA-256 is
325b6f26ca9452fcfb81cc6f52e3889573a7c141e9d07ab35f678b7d95d48e52.

This copy is modified, and the modifications are Rook's. scripts/build-sdk.sh
takes an upstream checkout, applies the two patches in patches/, and builds the
result. Each patch is small and readable:

  patches/0001-linux-clipboard.patch
      adds a Linux clipboard backend (src/linux-clipboard.ts) and wires
      src/clipboard.ts to it, so page.keyboard.paste works on Linux, which
      upstream did not support; plus its tests.
  patches/0002-vendor-build-root.patch
      lets scripts/build.mjs find the skills directory when the package is
      built outside a git checkout, via EGO_BROWSER_BUILD_ROOT.

The built bundle is not committed to this repository (vendor/ is ignored);
`scripts/build-sdk.sh` regenerates it, and vendor/UPSTREAM records which commit
it came from.

4. What Rook does not contain
=============================

Rook contains no code, strings, assets or UI copy from any closed-source
application. It is an independent program that implements a published protocol,
documented by the upstream project above, and it was checked against a build of
the app it is compatible with: docs/provenance.md records the audit, its probe
count and its result.

